// MEASUREMENT: the whole creation stat pool spent on Integrity.
//
// The Integrity half of a two-file pair — `player-points-atk.ron` and
// `player-points-integrity.ron` — identical in every field but
// `character.stats`. `player-points-atk.ron` carries the argument, the
// commands and the 2026-09-01 numbers; this file is its other row, and the
// full write-up is
// `docs/measurements/2026-09-01-creation-stat-pool-exchange-rates.md`.
//
//     cargo run --bin arena -- dev-arenas/player-points-integrity.ron
//
// The one thing worth reading off this row rather than that one: **the
// `companions down` column.** At 1000 reps this build put it at 1.28 against
// Attack's 1.04 and an unspent control's 1.17 — Integrity buys the player
// rounds, and those are rounds the pack also spends swinging at the party.
// A win rate alone hides that, and it is the reason "tankier is safer" is
// not simply true for a party of three.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 5, zone: 1),
    character: (
        stats: (0, 0, 9, 0),
    ),
    party: [
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
    ],
    opponents: [
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
    ],
    reps: 1000,
    seed: 1,
)
